# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unanchored on purpose. `/target` only matched the workspace root, so stray
# target/ dirs created by running cargo inside crates/ibex-config and fuzz put
# 79 MB into the index before anyone noticed.
target/
**/*.rs.bk
**/*.rmeta
# agent sessions have dropped libshared_*.rlib in the repo root
**/*.rlib
**/*.profraw
**/*.profdata

# A workspace member must not carry its own Cargo.lock -- it is a sign someone
# ran cargo inside the crate directory rather than at the root, which is also
# how the stray target/ dirs appeared.
crates/*/Cargo.lock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Profiling and capture artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `perf record` writes perf.data into the working directory. T39 left a 107 MB
# one in the repo root and it rejected a push of 49 unrelated files, because
# GitLab refuses blobs over 100 MB.
perf.data
perf.data.old
*.perf
# cargo-flamegraph's default output path
/flamegraph.svg
/perf.svg
*.pcap
*.pcapng
core
core.[0-9]*
vgcore.*
massif.out.*
*.heaptrace

# Checked-in flamegraphs under tools/ are deliverables and stay tracked; these
# patterns only catch the ones that land wherever a tool happened to run.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENTS.md rule 4 says temporary files go to /tmp. These patterns are the
# backstop for when that is not followed, which so far is most rounds.
/fix_*.py
/add_*.py
/insert_*.py
/modify*.py
/*_fix.py
/patch.py
/measure_*.sh
/run_*.sh
/clippy_output.json
/out.json
/results.json
/strace_*.txt
/*_build_time.txt
/size_measure.rs
/test_*.rs
# throwaway crates/**/scratch*.rs used to probe a dependency
**/scratch*.rs
# agy session registry and logs; machine state, not source
.agy/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Standalone tool crates (outside the workspace, so they carry their own state)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tools/allocprofile/target
/tools/allocprofile/Cargo.lock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and platform noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Flamegraphs, regenerated by tools/measure and tools/parity-bench on every run.
# A pair is ~700 KB and changes completely between runs, so they are diff noise.
# haproxy.svg and ibex.svg were tracked for a while before this rule existed; they
# are untracked now, so scope the rule to the two tools that emit them rather than
# ignoring every .svg and surprising whoever adds a real diagram later.
flame-*.svg
/tools/parity-bench/*.svg
/tools/measure/*.svg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fuzzing (cargo fuzz in fuzz/libfuzzer): the corpus grows by thousands of files
# per run and its own Cargo.lock is generated; neither belongs in the index.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
fuzz/libfuzzer/corpus/
fuzz/libfuzzer/Cargo.lock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local only: the operator's agent-session launchers, and the old WIP patch
# exports (2026-09-27; their work is on main or in the agy/T* branches).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/agy-resume.sh
/mythos-resume.sh
/claude-vv-resume.sh
/patches/
